WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.603 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.738
-Hello, everybody,
and welcome to "Corrections,"

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:10.110
week of Tuesday, August 17th.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.079
I feel like we always
overvalue Monday.

00:00:14.079 --> 00:00:18.183
Tuesday was just as important
in making this a week.

00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:20.019
Let's start with the fact

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:24.691
that I complained that
Vince Vaughn wasn't in "Loki."

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.593
I thought it would be great

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.227
if he and Owen Wilson
were in "Loki" together.

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:30.830
And plus, he could then say,
"Buddy, buddy, buddy,"

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.766
because there
were three Lokis.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.800
And then we showed a picture,
and a lot of you pointed out

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.036
that the photo we showed,
there were actually four Lokis

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:40.406
because there was
Alligator Loki.

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.308
The problem is,

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:45.045
my Vaughn only works
with three "buddies."

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.715
"Buddy, buddy, buddy" --
that's Vince Vaughn.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:52.485
"Buddy, buddy, buddy, buddy" --
it could be anyone.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.357
I said "PIN number."

00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:01.360
The "N" in PIN is "number."

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.195
So when I say PIN number,

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:06.833
I'm saying personal
identification number number.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.834
It was an error.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:12.138
Or an homage!

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:16.242
To my favorite "Goodfellas"
character, Johnny Two Times.

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.144
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:25.518
We talked about cliff diving.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.853
I talked about wearing
a squirrel suit

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:30.356
to go cliff diving,
then I got correct and I said

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.025
I meant to say BASE diving.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:35.461
It's BASE jumping.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:36.796
BASE is an acronym.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.798
Do you know what it stands for,
Shoemaker?

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.000
-Nope.
-Why do I come to you?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.036
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.676
It's the four things you can
jump off.

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:52.378
BASE is buildings; antennae;

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:55.381
spans, meaning bridges;

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.418
and earth, meaning cliffs.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:06.459
Alright, there's a poll,
a company, an organization --

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.194
I don't even know
what they are --

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.230
Quinnipiac.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.732
I think I said Quinni-PI-ac.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:19.405
So here's what I want you to do.
Quin-NI-piac or Quinni-PI-ac.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.006
I need everybody
to take out their phones.

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:24.177
If you think the first one
was right, press 1.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.379
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:38.457
We talked about flutes and how
there are no left-handed flutes.

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:39.959
So people said to me,

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.129
there actually -- there are
left-handed flutes.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:46.432
They're expensive,
but there's a company, Viento.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:50.236
A couple of people said
Viento makes them.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.004
So I looked it up,
and there is a company,

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:55.674
a German company, Viento,
that makes left-handed flutes.

00:02:55.674 --> 00:02:57.710
They're not a sponsor.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:00.914
Okay, this is not --

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.715
we've never had a sponsor
in "Corrections."

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:05.652
That's not what this is about.
But I did think it would be fun.

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.855
I would like to.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:13.092
Maybe I'll just do
an ad for them

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:18.164
and then with the hopes that
they just have a massive week.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.899
Right? They sell more --

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:23.102
Like, the left-handed flutes are
just flying off the shelves.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.603
Then they'll come back to us

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:25.938
and say, "Oh, my God,
that was great,"

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:28.308
and then we'll have them
over a barrel.

00:03:30.976 --> 00:03:32.912
"A newcomer to the United States
instrument market,

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.415
Viento flutes are a fine value
for the money.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.484
These flutes are designed
for entry-level flutists

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.052
and are built to take
the challenges

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:42.054
that a young owner
can present a flute."

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:45.891
Very eggy language there.

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:48.728
I double-checked
before I said it

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.897
'cause I thought
it was "flautists."

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:51.964
Either work.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:55.735
Flutist or flautist
are the same.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:58.905
So, a flutist
would sound like this.

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:01.908
[ Flute trills ]

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.577
And a flautist would sound
like this.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:07.580
[ Flute trills ]

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.416
And a flatulist
would sound like this.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:11.918
[ Fart noise ]

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.953
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:22.928
That is base humor,

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:24.430
which means...

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.600
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.435
...it's funny in a building...

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.104
[ Laughs ]

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:36.375
Oh, I misspoke.
I just said a word wrong.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.645
I said that Mike Lindell
was a pillow magnet.

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:41.681
He's a pillow magnate.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:44.584
He is a lawsuit magnet.

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:47.586
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.586 --> 00:04:50.622
I also said that My Pillows --

00:04:50.622 --> 00:04:53.258
as a joke --
I jokingly said they were filled

00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:57.196
with rock-hard calcified turds.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:05:00.667
Which people told me
there's a word for -- coprolite.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.802
It's not a correction; that was
just like a helpful, like,

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.904
"Hey, Seth,
here's some new vocab for you."

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.739
So, coprolite.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.073
And I should stress,

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:11.744
they are not filled
with rock-hard calcified turds.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.512
And just out of good faith,

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:15.581
I went on the
My Pillow website today

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:18.083
to try to find out
what they were filled with.

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:20.519
Could not find out.

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:23.021
Not a helpful website.

00:05:23.021 --> 00:05:25.391
With everything else.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:27.126
This is true.
This was in the FAQs.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:29.361
I went to the FAQs
on the website

00:05:29.361 --> 00:05:31.798
trying to find out
what's in a My Pillow.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:34.367
There were only six.
There were only six FAQs.

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:38.604
One was, "Can I get My Pillow
in Canada?"

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:41.341
You've been frequently
asked that?

00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:45.878
This one was very --
it said,

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.647
"How do I know
what pillow I have?"

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:50.115
This is a frequently
asked question.

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:55.188
"Yellow will have yellow
writing on the tag.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:59.959
White will have black
writing on the tag.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:03.495
Green will have green
writing on the tag.

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:08.000
Blue will have blue
writing on the tag."

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.803
I don't know why they did
a white one

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:13.972
that had black
writing on the tab.

00:06:13.972 --> 00:06:16.976
Starting to think this guy
and I think differently.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:20.346
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:23.615
Also, a lot of people have said,

00:06:23.615 --> 00:06:26.953
based on my impression
of Mike Lindell,

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:31.490
"Hey, he's not from Chicago.
He's from Minnesota.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:36.929
Stop making him sound like
one of the SNL Super Fans."

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:41.400
And he is from Minnesota, but
I learned a lesson this year.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:45.304
And that lesson is, sometimes
what you want to be true

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:49.175
is more important than
what is actually true.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:51.878
And I learned that
from Mike Lindell.

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:59.652
I talked about this last week

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:02.287
'cause this was
in last week's correction,

00:07:02.287 --> 00:07:04.823
that if Rudy had been told

00:07:04.823 --> 00:07:08.194
to book a press conference
at the Waldorf Astoria,

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:10.896
he would book it
at a Walmart in Astoria.

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:13.832
A lot of people said there is
not a Walmart in Astoria.

00:07:13.832 --> 00:07:15.000
I corrected myself.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.437
Then some people from Oregon
were like,

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:21.974
"Hey, there's an Astoria
in Oregon that has a Walmart."

00:07:23.842 --> 00:07:25.177
So, because we...

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:29.648
Look, when we can,
we will fix the problem.

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:34.186
We will go back
and re-edit "A Closer Look."

00:07:34.186 --> 00:07:35.688
So, if you were
to go back now,

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:37.022
this is what you would see.

00:07:37.022 --> 00:07:39.525
I'm at the Walmart in
[overdubbed] Astoria, Oregon.

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:42.295
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.632 --> 00:07:49.301
Also, I did double-check.

00:07:49.301 --> 00:07:52.404
I don't know if it's actually
in Astoria, Oregon.

00:07:52.404 --> 00:07:56.175
It's in Warrenton, Oregon,
which is next door.

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:58.644
So this is a true question
I'm asking

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.312
for our Ore-gone-ian --

00:08:00.312 --> 00:08:01.847
Ore-go-nian --

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:04.850
people in Oregon.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:07.286
People of Oregon, be honest.

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:11.090
If I said to you, "Meet me
at the Walmart in Astoria,"

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:14.026
would you know what I meant?

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:15.528
Press 1.

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:17.563
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.002
I talked about my contest
with Lorde

00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:24.737
about who's a better painter,

00:08:24.737 --> 00:08:26.338
and I said that I moved the poll

00:08:26.338 --> 00:08:28.608
from the "Late Night"
Twitter account

00:08:28.608 --> 00:08:32.211
to the Sea Captain Polls
Twitter account

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:35.981
because I thought there would be
less Lorde fans there.

00:08:35.981 --> 00:08:39.551
Fewer Lorde fans there.

00:08:39.551 --> 00:08:45.124
Although I also hope they were,
like, just less fans of hers.

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:49.262
Like, still fans, just a little
bit less, and that would...

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:51.196
Okay.

00:08:51.196 --> 00:08:53.365
We talked about
"Prince of Tides"

00:08:53.365 --> 00:08:55.601
and how I had late fees

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:58.137
because I rented
"Prince of Tides"

00:08:58.137 --> 00:09:02.274
from Blockbuster
when I was 18 years old.

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:06.779
And I said, "Yeah,
I rented it when I was 18.

00:09:06.779 --> 00:09:10.382
I was one of the kids who liked
watching 'Prince of Tides.'"

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:12.885
And somebody -- a bunch of
people said, "If you were 18,

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:15.153
you weren't a kid."

00:09:15.153 --> 00:09:17.155
And now here's the crazy thing.

00:09:17.155 --> 00:09:18.724
We had originally written
the joke to say,

00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:21.760
"When I was 17,
I rented 'Prince of Tides,'"

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:23.362
so I would have been fine.

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:29.501
This is an actual email
we got from our fact-checker,

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:31.836
noting that
"Seth would have turned 18

00:09:31.836 --> 00:09:33.205
on December 28, 1991.

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:34.973
'Prince of Tides'
was released in theaters

00:09:34.973 --> 00:09:36.408
Christmas Day 1991.

00:09:36.408 --> 00:09:39.144
Unless he somehow got a bootleg
VHS in those three days,

00:09:39.144 --> 00:09:41.147
which Blockbuster would
not have been renting,

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:42.815
he would have had to rent
'Prince of Tides'

00:09:42.815 --> 00:09:45.484
when he was over 18, in 1992."

00:09:45.484 --> 00:09:48.988
The jackals are
inside the house.

00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:51.090
[ Laughter ]

00:09:57.162 --> 00:09:59.465
I also said it was $60,000
in late fees.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:00.766
A lot of people
took issue with that.

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:02.568
They said it was a dollar
a day at Blockbuster

00:10:02.568 --> 00:10:03.969
and there was a cap.

00:10:03.969 --> 00:10:05.504
And even if it was a dollar
a day and there was no cap,

00:10:05.504 --> 00:10:07.172
it wouldn't have been $60,000.

00:10:07.172 --> 00:10:09.775
But then someone else said,
yeah, but Blockbuster,

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:11.610
what they did was
they actually turned over

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.812
all the late fees
to a collection agency.

00:10:13.812 --> 00:10:15.781
So it wasn't Blockbuster
trying to get the money.

00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:17.182
It was a collection agency.

00:10:17.182 --> 00:10:19.318
And that made sense to me
because I remember once

00:10:19.318 --> 00:10:20.819
a few years ago -- and again,

00:10:20.819 --> 00:10:22.187
I still had
'Prince of Tides,' right?

00:10:22.187 --> 00:10:23.956
I hadn't returned it.
I'm in the grocery store.

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:25.590
I'm in, like,
the produce section.

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:29.595
And there's just this guy, this,
like, hulking guy next to me

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:31.797
in the produce section -- he's
just sort of looking over at me.

00:10:31.797 --> 00:10:33.632
And finally I look over
and I make eye contact

00:10:33.632 --> 00:10:38.370
and he's like, "How you doing?
You okay? You okay?"

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.740 align:end size:94% position:94%
And I say, "Yeah, I'm fine."
He goes, "That's good.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.941
'Cause I got a friend,
he's not okay.

00:10:42.941 --> 00:10:44.710
Eh, he's not okay."

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:46.278
And I'm like,
"Oh, I'm sorry to hear that."

00:10:46.278 --> 00:10:48.580
He goes, "Yeah.
His name's Tom Wingo.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.115
You ever heard of Tom Wingo?"

00:10:50.115 --> 00:10:52.250
And I had, because that's
Nick Nolte's character's name

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:54.419
in "Prince of Tides."

00:10:54.419 --> 00:10:55.754
But, you know, obviously,

00:10:55.754 --> 00:10:57.089
I'm starting to get
a little worried.

00:10:57.089 --> 00:10:59.725
I'm like, "I don't think
I have heard of Tom Wingo."

00:10:59.725 --> 00:11:03.128
He goes, "Yeah, that's funny,
because I heard you had.

00:11:03.128 --> 00:11:06.265
I heard you had
heard about him.

00:11:06.265 --> 00:11:08.768
And I want to check up on him,
see what he's done,

00:11:08.768 --> 00:11:11.002
see if he's come back
from New York City,

00:11:11.002 --> 00:11:14.239
moved back to Charleston.

00:11:14.239 --> 00:11:16.775
But I can't, 'cause
you got the tape!"

00:11:16.775 --> 00:11:19.778
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.778 --> 00:11:22.781
[ Laughing ] And I had to
give him 60 grand.

00:11:22.781 --> 00:11:25.717
We said that Donald Trump
looked tired the other day

00:11:25.717 --> 00:11:27.820
and we said he looked like

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:29.221
he accidentally reached
for a Diet Coke,

00:11:29.221 --> 00:11:32.257
but had Sudafed instead.
Many of you said Sudafed --

00:11:32.257 --> 00:11:35.593
I should have said Nyquil
because Sudafed is like

00:11:35.593 --> 00:11:37.162
basically an amphetamine.

00:11:37.162 --> 00:11:40.766
And that's why you need
to show ID to get Sudafed,

00:11:40.766 --> 00:11:45.070
because a lot of people
use it illicitly.

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:49.141
And that made sense to me
because I feel like the energy

00:11:49.141 --> 00:11:53.145
of those of you
who leave comments --

00:11:53.145 --> 00:11:55.814
it has, like, a meth-y energy.

00:11:55.814 --> 00:11:58.584
[ Laughter ]

00:11:58.584 --> 00:12:02.320
Like that you're all
cranked up on ice.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.491
"Should we watch 'Closer Look'
again and look for flubs?"

00:12:09.728 --> 00:12:12.598
Pundit.
We say pundit a lot.

00:12:12.598 --> 00:12:16.034
And I don't know why --
I do say "pundint."

00:12:16.034 --> 00:12:18.970
And I got to stop doing it.
It's wrong.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:21.440
I have no defense of it.
I will say...

00:12:23.608 --> 00:12:26.979
I wish it was "pundint" so that
when they were wrong --

00:12:26.979 --> 00:12:29.347
'cause I think a lot of pundits
go on the cable news shows

00:12:29.347 --> 00:12:30.549
and when they come on,

00:12:30.549 --> 00:12:32.284
a lot of the things
they say are wrong.

00:12:32.284 --> 00:12:35.454
It would be fun, like
six months after the fact,

00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:37.989
to do --
you could do like a series.

00:12:37.989 --> 00:12:42.061
You could do a feature on your
show, a recurring segment

00:12:42.061 --> 00:12:44.830
where you would have
a pundit on,

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.699
if they were called
"pundints" --

00:12:46.699 --> 00:12:48.800
again, this is me just being
wishful thinking --

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.535
where you would show them
something they had said

00:12:50.535 --> 00:12:52.370
that they'd gotten wrong,
and you could call it

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:54.373
"Oh, No, You Pundint!"

00:13:01.079 --> 00:13:02.748
Emmy voting is open.

00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:04.916
This is an Emmy-nominated
piece of content.

00:13:04.916 --> 00:13:07.953
We've talked about this.
What we have not talked about

00:13:07.953 --> 00:13:10.789
are our fellow nominees
in the category,

00:13:10.789 --> 00:13:15.460
all of whom we would be
honored to lose to.

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:18.130
Randy Rainbow,
such a funny gentleman.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:20.632
You can check him out
on YouTube.

00:13:20.632 --> 00:13:23.168
"Carpool Karaoke" -- as good
a recurring segment

00:13:23.168 --> 00:13:25.504
on any late-night talk show
in the last decade.

00:13:25.504 --> 00:13:28.007
They have a show on Apple.

00:13:28.007 --> 00:13:30.475
That's with our friend
James Corden.

00:13:30.475 --> 00:13:33.812
"Tooning Out the News" is
this incredibly inventive

00:13:33.812 --> 00:13:36.782
cartoon political interview show

00:13:36.782 --> 00:13:39.050
that Stephen Colbert
produces -- fantastic.

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:41.253
You kind of have to see it
to believe it.

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:42.387
Do search that out.

00:13:42.387 --> 00:13:43.755
And "Reno 911!"

00:13:43.755 --> 00:13:46.592
which was a fantastic show
for years on Comedy Central

00:13:46.592 --> 00:13:49.895
and had a new season
on Quibi.

00:13:49.895 --> 00:13:54.900
And Thomas Lennon and others,
our friends did that show.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:58.403
And so, you know,
all wonderful shows.

00:13:58.403 --> 00:14:04.076
And I don't know if I'm the
right person to say this, but...

00:14:04.076 --> 00:14:07.079
I think it's pretty cool
that I mentioned them.

00:14:07.079 --> 00:14:10.783
[ Laughter ]

00:14:10.783 --> 00:14:13.318
You know?

00:14:13.318 --> 00:14:15.020
Didn't have to.

00:14:17.055 --> 00:14:18.690
I don't know, I'm just
saying, like --

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:21.727
like, I'm me,

00:14:21.727 --> 00:14:24.763
so I can't say, but I feel like
if I wasn't me right now,

00:14:24.763 --> 00:14:26.932
I would be like, "Alright!"

00:14:26.932 --> 00:14:29.134
[ Laughter ]

00:14:33.172 --> 00:14:40.512
But so anyway, I think
all five are just super.

00:14:40.512 --> 00:14:44.015
But, you know, the only thing
I'll say is, like...

00:14:44.015 --> 00:14:46.886
you know,
we did this together, guys.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.192
Alright. See you next week.

